{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`autodeploy.sh`'s `MCP_PATHS` delta gate does not include `SECRETS_PATHS`. A change that touches\nONLY `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh` or `infra/terraform/ssm.tf` therefore does not trigger an\nmcp redeploy, so newly-emitted `.env` values never reach the running mcp container. The container\nkeeps serving with a stale environment and nothing reports a problem.\n\n## Why it is not theoretical\n\nThis is the SAME CLASS as the gap already fixed for the review-bot (the `f600` / incident-2731\nwork), which is why `SECRETS_PATHS` exists as a distinct variable in the first place — the bot's\ndelta gate was taught to watch it. The mcp block was never given the same treatment.\n\nIt becomes reachable the moment a secrets-only change lands. Concretely: the Jira wiring under\n`colourless-hasteless-lamb` adds four `JIRA_*` emissions to `fetch-secrets.sh`. That change also\ntouches `docker-compose.yml` (which IS in `MCP_PATHS`), so it happens to redeploy — but a FOLLOW-UP\nthat adjusts only the fetch-secrets side, or an SSM value rotation handled by re-running\nfetch-secrets, would silently not reach the container.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:168` — `SECRETS_PATHS='infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh infra/terraform/ssm.tf'`\n- The bot block's delta gate consults it; the mcp block's `changed_range \"$mcp_deployed\" \"$TARGET\" \"$MCP_PATHS\"`\n  does not.\n\n## Note on a pure SSM VALUE rotation\n\nA rotation that changes only the SSM value and no git path is out of scope for a git-delta gate\nby construction — no commit exists to detect. That case needs its own mechanism (or an operator\naction) and should NOT be conflated with this bug, which is specifically about a committed\nsecrets change failing to redeploy mcp.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A commit touching only `SECRETS_PATHS` triggers an mcp redeploy, so refreshed `.env` values\n      reach the container.\n- [ ] A test asserts the mcp delta gate covers `SECRETS_PATHS`, mirroring the review-bot's.\n- [ ] The pure-SSM-value-rotation case is documented as out of scope with its actual remedy named.\n- [ ] LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE. Observed on the box: a secrets-only deploy is followed\n      by an mcp container whose environment carries the new value. Record the autodeploy journal\n      lines and the container identity in a ticket comment.\n\n## Found by\n\nThe subagent wiring `colourless-hasteless-lamb`, as an adjacent gap it correctly declined to fix\nin scope.\n\n---\n\n## Confirmed root cause (see the RCA comment for the full experiment log)\n\nProven at runtime by driving the shipped `autodeploy.sh` against a real git repo whose only\nchanged file is a secrets path: the tick builds and restarts the review-bot, logs\n\"deploy complete\", stamps the target sha — and never emits `compose-build-mcp` or\n`run --name rebar-mcp-…`. The delta is consumed and never retried.\n\nThe rival explanation \"the bot's own fetch-secrets refresh covers mcp\" is ruled out: that\nrefresh (`autodeploy.sh:667`) does rewrite the shared on-disk `.env`, but mcp reads `.env` and\n`mcp-static-tokens.json` once at container init (`mcp_run_new`'s `--env-file` and read-only\nbind-mount, `:370-408`), so without a NEW container the running server keeps the old values.\n`infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md:200` states the same restart requirement independently.\n\n## Fix plan\n\n1. Add an `mcp_delta()` helper beside `changed()` in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` that returns\n   true when EITHER `MCP_PATHS` or `SECRETS_PATHS` changed over `$mcp_deployed..$TARGET`, with a\n   comment naming why mcp is the other consumer of fetch-secrets output.\n2. Call it from BOTH mcp gate sites — the backoff-active arm and the backoff-clear arm — so a\n   secrets-only delta is reported as pending during a backoff window instead of being dropped.\n   Mirrors the review-bot gate, which has ORed `SECRETS_PATHS` since f600 / incident 2731.\n3. Annotate the canonical `MCP_PATHS` declaration in the `mcp:` compose service comment\n   (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`) so the two declarations do not drift.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_secrets_only_change_redeploys_mcp`, parametrized over `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh` and\n`infra/terraform/ssm.tf`, on the existing real-bash `_real_git_box` harness (`ssm.tf` added to\nits repo baseline). It asserts BOTH that mcp is rebuilt AND that a new mcp container is started\n— refreshing the files on disk without a new container is precisely the non-fix.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\nA pure SSM VALUE rotation advances no git ref, so no git-delta gate can observe it — by\nconstruction, not by omission. That path stays operator-driven via\n`infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`. This change is not a substitute for it, and the ticket's\nAC3 is satisfied by naming that remedy rather than by extending the gate.\n\n## Note on AC4 (live validation)\n\nAC4 requires observing a secrets-only deploy on the box. This change is authored under a\nread-only-box constraint, so AC4 is NOT satisfied here and the ticket must not be closed on this\nchange alone: it needs an operator to observe the next secrets-only deploy and record the\njournal lines and container identity."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787953108457457001,"uuid":"f6e24c89-0875-4c6c-97e7-baf8fab02cd5"}